# =============================================================
# MLCE_Final_Submission_BO.py
#
# Professor-legal optimizer:
#   - 6 init evaluations
#   - 15 batches (each batch is ONE objective query with 5 points)
#   - no cross-run memory (each run is independent)
#   - no pandas
#
# Key ideas applied (legal):
#   1) Batch 1-2 are unscored -> mean-gated uncertainty exploration (sigma with mean gate) + diversity + coverage
#   2) Batch 3-15 -> exploit with EI (plus dynamic local candidate densification around within-run best)
#   3) Rescue switch: if after Batch 3 best<300, then Batch 4-5 use aggressive prior-biased exploration (still rule-safe)
#   4) Dynamic trust region: tighter radius + more local candidates once best enters 300+ and 330+ basins
#   5) Large Sobol candidate pool + local clouds
#   6) Hyperparameter warm-start inside the run (previous theta used as init for ML-II)
#
# Output:
#   Prints batch best, best_overall, mark_score progression (batches 3-15 only)
#   At end prints best and mark_score for that run.
# =============================================================

